sers, grants and the loopback IdP are synthetic and approve nothing. Disclosed: corrective_case stays audited and unmeasured (ADR-0064 A4.5, D-264); A4.9 residuals 1 and 4 not exercised. screen_api corrected per D-250 O6: reports are in the DO-D/DO-E handback evidence and QA-C's test-evidence/DG7/qa/. QA-C's independent re-run is in progress at this pass. DG7 analyst pass 7 (T-DG7-AN-P7G, base 5458273, 2026-11-16; F-DG7-921): correction of the evidence for 'records, jobs and approvals intact after a full restart'. The DO-D8 and DO-D8B handbacks found (DO-D8 §4, DO-D8B §4) that before DO-D8 the drill's stop of PostgreSQL sent SIGTERM only to pg_start's launcher subshell, so the D9 runs of DO-D7 and DO-E (and QA round-2 A18) most probably did not restart PostgreSQL itself: only the API and worker restarts were real. Their work trees are gone, so this is an inference from the measured mechanism, not a proof either way; those runs are kept above as history and are not the evidence for the full-restart clause. The evidence for that clause is DO-D8B's T-B11 run (docs/delivery/handbacks/DG7/T-DG7-DO-D8B-evidence/t-b11-run.log; driver exit 0, D0-D11 PASS): its D9 step runs 'stop worker; ... stop API, PostgreSQL; start PostgreSQL, API, worker; job-check compare; ...', job-check reports 'PASS: enabled schedules equal, earlier job_run rows unchanged (0 new), approval rows equal', the export queued before the restart completes after it with equal SHA-256, 2 evidence downloads have equal SHA-256, reconcile after use matches, and D9 PASS in 9.573 s. In that drill code (deploy/scripts/transfer-drill.sh, D9: td_stop_pg on the postmaster and td_stop_pg_dir on pgT/data, else 'D9: the target PostgreSQL did not stop before its restart' and FAIL) a PASS requires the old postmaster to have stopped; that line is absent from the log. The log itself prints no postmaster pid or shutdown line, so the real stop rests on that code path plus the PASS. The drill code is unchanged from DO-D8B's base 7c819f08c to this base (git diff empty). DO-D8's own T-B11 (T-DG7-DO-D8-evidence/t-b11-run.log) also shows D9 PASS after the fix, but its driver ended with exit 2 (cleanup, F-DG7-963), so it is not cited as the primary run. Acceptance still met; status unchanged."
